# Day 59 – Launch & Production Readiness

## Objective
Prepare the application for public release by completing final launch checks, verifying deployment, updating documentation, and ensuring the live version is production-ready.

## What I Completed
- Completed the final release readiness review.
- Verified deployment and environment configuration.
- Performed end-to-end testing on the live application.
- Confirmed the deployed version matches the local build.
- Fixed remaining production issues.
- Updated README and project documentation.
- Captured screenshots of the final deployed application.
- Created the final launch commit and pushed all changes to GitHub.

## Key Learnings
- Launch is more than deployment—it includes documentation, testing, and reliability.
- Production readiness requires verifying every workflow.
- A polished, stable product creates a better user experience.
- Final testing increases confidence before public release.

## Deliverables
- Live deployed application
- Updated GitHub repository
- Final documentation
- Launch-ready product
